# Level 3 (reached on turn 1): "If you would put one or more counters ... put twice that many". The Talent's own combat trigger puts a +1/+1 counter on Bot1's Ornithopter and it gets two. On turn 2 Bot2's Bristly Bill puts a counter
# on that same Ornithopter (landfall, Bot2's Forest) and Bot2 is the one putting it, so it is not doubled: three counters in all. (The Ornithopter has a counter, so level 2's ward {1} makes Bot2 pay {1} for the trigger, which it does with the Forest.)

